					"text": "tap.python.spike-q3-dumpout\n\nQ3 (M1): get<attr> through the obex-stored dumpout. 'getsteps' should output 'steps 5' and, after 'steps 8', 'steps 8' to q3-dumpout \u2014 unless the class's anything takes it (the console would say 'spike: class anything received'). Compared with the class attribute 'level' (getlevel), with object_attr_getdump() called directly (getdump), and with what object_attr_method() resolves each message to (attrmethod) \u2014 on [tap.python], whose class registers object_obex_dumpout() as its dumpout method as the SDK's examples do, and on [tap.python.spike.nodumpout], the same class without it.",
